cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, you are required by its license to cite it. Use the metadata below."
title: "32k-XAI: Mechanistic simulation of 32,000 cognitive agents"
abstract: >-
  A research platform for simulating a synthetic population of 32,000
  autonomous cognitive agents, each governed by a transparent,
  mechanistically interpretable decision architecture parameterized by
  empirically grounded psychological variables. Enables causal, glass-box
  interrogation of emergent social phenomena by tracing macro-level
  outcomes to specific cognitive parameters at the individual level.
  No neural networks. No large language models. Every decision traceable
  to a named parameter with documented uncertainty and provenance.
